c:physics","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-04-27T09:36:23Z","updated_at":"2026-04-27T12:04:02Z","closed_at":"2026-04-27T10:19:21Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproductible in Godot 4.6.2 stable.mono\n- Reproductible in Godot 4.7 beta-1.mono\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9597) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.94 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n### Setup\nI'm currently working on a **2D** platformer game where one of its **core** mechanic is to send the player in the background. In that regard, I've created  a Parallax2D node, in which I've added a **TilemapLayer** node for the floor. I also added in 4 **AnimatableBody2D** platforms, with **`one-way collision`** and **`Sync to Physics`** enabled. \n\nScene setup : \n\n<img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e9690d16-0815-4214-87f6-29ed963c9d31\" />\n\n---\n### Issues\nFirst, when **`Sync_to_physics`** is enabled for the platforms and the game is run, the platforms are offseted without any obvious reason. Moreover, when I try to jump on top of the platforms, my character goes through them as if there wasn't no collision. The collision is also offseted and appears to be a \"ghost\" collision. See the video below : \n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f3422210-2fc9-4213-a99d-d565405eb9cc\n\nNow, if I uncheck **`Sync_to_physics`**, there is no more offset and platform collision works as expected. But when my character lands on top of it, \nthere is a strange acceleration applied to the character, even if no input is applied. Look at the video : \n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fe125433-bc59-4669-a002-f4ef55848b37\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAll you have to do is run the project an test. Its a very small project.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThis is the MRP : \n\n[parallax(v.4.6)_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27119840/parallax.v.4.6._mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"SilverWolveGames","id":92260598,"node_id":"U_kgDOBX_I9g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92260598?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames","html_url":"https://github.com/SilverWolveGames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118994/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket"